.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_REPLACE_DATA 3 2026-09-28 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_replace_data \- stage a named replacement from memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.B "int32_t libmpq__patch_replace_data("
.B "        mpq_patch_s *patch, const char *filename,"
.B "        const uint8_t *data, libmpq__off_t size,"
.B "        const mpq_file_options_s *options"
.B ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stages a replacement for an existing named base member using \fIsize\fP bytes from \fIdata\fP. It does not modify the base archive or publish the patch. The private writer selects a validated BSD0 delta only when smaller than a whole-file PTCH COPY payload. NULL \fIoptions\fP selects patch-writer defaults. Explicit options control storage of the patch member, not the final patched file; locale and platform must match the base member. Add and rename operations are not supported.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A missing member or invalid pointer returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Locale/platform mismatches or unsupported options return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. Size, allocation, decoding, and I/O errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__patch_replace_path (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_finish (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_add_data (3)
